  "text_conditions": {
    "reference": "The drinking age in the United States is generally 21, as mandated by the Drinking Age Act of 1984. However, several states briefly lowered the age to 18 or 19 before raising it again, such as Alaska (1970 to 1984), Arizona (1972 to 1985), and Connecticut (1972 to 1985). Some states have specific exemptions, like Connecticut allowing consumption with parental supervision or for religious ceremonies in California."
